    "file": "harfbuzz/src/OT/Layout/GSUB/SubstLookup.hh",
    "description": "`SubstLookup::is_reverse()` assumes every GSUB Extension lookup has at least one subtable and unconditionally calls `get_subtable(0)`. GSUB sanitization accepts a Lookup whose `lookupType` is Extension and whose `subTable.len` is zero: the generic array sanitizer accepts the empty array, and the extension consistency check in `Lookup::sanitize()` is explicitly guarded by `subtables &&`. During shaping, `apply_string()` calls `lookup.is_reverse()`, which indexes the nonexistent first offset; `Lookup::get_subtable()` then reads an `Offset16` beyond the sanitized table/blob, causing the heap-buffer-overflow in the big-endian integer conversion. The vulnerable runtime function must handle an empty extension lookup (or sanitization must reject this combination) before accessing subtable zero.",
    "conditions": "A crafted font supplied through the shape-fuzzer must contain a GSUB lookup selected by the shaping plan with lookup type `Extension` (GSUB type 7), but a zero subtable count, positioned so the nonexistent first offset lies outside the GSUB blob. The table passes current GSUB sanitization because zero-length subtable arrays are allowed and no extension-type consistency read occurs when the count is zero. Shaping a nonempty buffer with an active lookup mask reaches `apply_string()`, which invokes `is_reverse()` and performs the out-of-bounds read before lookup application."
